        "rationale": "The requirement only constrains what the review prompt says. \"MUST include at least one worked example of a mechanical change and at least one worked example of a design question\" and \"The mechanical example MUST show a flawed draft together with the change the reviewer makes to it\" both describe document content. They do not prescribe libraries, types, signatures, delegation or algorithms. Any prompt layout that has those examples would meet them, so no clause is a structural obligation.\n\nThe root `assets/skills/habeas-requirements/references/review-prompt.md`, in `section[Requirement group review]/section[Examples]`, also contains the content:\n- Mechanical example: a flawed compound draft is quoted (\"The `refactor` command accepts file, node, and definition mappings, ...\"). The reviewer's change follows it: split it into `mappings.file`, `mappings.node`, and the other listed requirements, and \"Not a question.\" A second mechanical wording fix is also given.\n- Design question example: a quoted note about `rewrite.rationale`, with options (a), (b) and (c) and a recommendation.\n\nNo further implementation evidence is needed."
